# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_extractor_prisma.py" "PRISMA GATE: PASS" "Prisma ORM extractor (model declarations -> table nodes + cross-substrate crown jewel)" "Prisma schema.prisma model blocks mint table nodes and wire up the cross-substrate crown jewel: a SQL migration and a TS query file that both touch the same Prisma model name are coupled via the shared table node with NO import/call edge between them." "THE GAP FIXED: .prisma files were NOT in _SOURCE_EXT (never walked by the extractor) and _ORM_PATTERNS had no pattern for Prisma model blocks, so Prisma apps minted 0 table nodes. The cross-substrate crown jewel (migration alters T + TS code queries T + schema.prisma declares model T) was invisible. Prisma is the fastest-growing JS/TS ORM (4M+ weekly npm downloads) and the default ORM for Next.js/T3 -- the most popular full-stack JS framework -- making this the highest-impact single ORM gap remaining. TWO CHANGES: (1) code_graph_extract.py -- .prisma added to _SOURCE_EXT so schema files are walked and passed to the schema extractor; (2) _cg_schema.py -- model pattern added to _ORM_PATTERNS (anchored on the model keyword at a word boundary followed by an identifier and a literal brace) so each model block mints a table node; the routing guard in _schema_graph now passes .prisma files through the ORM path. PRECISION: enum/datasource/generator/type blocks each use their own keyword and are never matched by the model pattern; ordinary JS/TS/Python code that mentions the word model is safe because .prisma files are only walked for schema extraction. WHAT THIS GATE PROVES (hermetic, no DB, no Postgres, no network): (1) model User mints a table node named user; (2) a second model Post mints a second table node post; (3) enum Role does NOT mint a table node; (4) datasource db does NOT mint a table node; (5) generator client does NOT mint a table node; (6) cross-substrate crown jewel -- a SQL migration altering user and a TS file querying user are coupled via the shared user table node from schema.prisma with NO import/call edge between migration and TS file; (7) empty .prisma file does not crash; (8) content-free -- a secret embedded in a .prisma comment does not appear in the graph output. MEASURED on cal.com (real Prisma app): BEFORE 0 table nodes from .prisma files; AFTER 100 table nodes from .prisma files (101 models across 2 schema.prisma files, 100 distinct after normalization). 46 enums in the same schemas produce 0 table nodes (precision confirmed)." 20
